[2026-03-14T22:43:12.646Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0178jyNx5DhSddVzwJG9b4ur","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary of Linear-Clone App Exploration\n\n### 1. App Directory Structure\n\n**Top-level directories:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/` - main app directory\n- `src/` - source code\n- `tests/` - test files (.spec.ts)\n- `netlify/functions/` - backend API functions\n- `docs/` - documentation (tests.md)\n- `scripts/` - database seeding scripts\n- `public/` - static assets\n- `node_modules/` - dependencies\n- `logs/` - application logs\n\n**Key subdirectories:**\n- `src/components/` - React components (ProjectHeader.tsx, ProjectOverviewTab.tsx, etc.)\n- `src/pages/` - page components (ProjectDetail.tsx, Projects.tsx, etc.)\n- `src/slices/` - Redux slices for state management (projectDetailSlice.ts, etc.)\n- `netlify/functions/` - API endpoints\n\n---\n\n### 2. Tests Documentation (docs/tests.md) - Key Test Sections\n\n#### **Project Header Tests**\n- **Project header renders all fields** - Project name (inline-editable), status badge, progress bar (%), target date, lead with avatar\n- **Inline edit project name** - Click name, clear, type new name, press Enter or click away\n- **Inline edit project name — cancel edit** - Press Escape to revert\n- **Inline edit project name — validation** - Empty name validation error\n- **Inline edit status badge** - Dropdown with all statuses: \"Planned\", \"In Progress\", \"Completed\", \"Cancelled\"\n- **Change project status** - Updates badge with color styling, persists to DB, creates activity entry\n- **Status changes multiple times** - Sequential changes both persist separately\n\n#### **Target Date Tests**\n- **Inline edit target date via date picker** - Click opens date picker with current date pre-selected\n- **Change target date** - Select new date, updates display, persists, activity entry created\n- **Clear target date** - Remove option available, shows \"No target date\" placeholder\n\n#### **Lead Tests**\n- **Inline edit lead via searchable selector** - Click opens searchable dropdown with all workspace members\n- **Change project lead** - Type to search, select member, updates with avatar, persists, activity entry\n- **Search lead selector filters results** - Typing filters members\n- **Remove project lead** - Unassign option, shows \"No lead\" placeholder\n\n#### **Progress Bar Tests**\n- **Progress bar reflects issue completion** - Shows percentage filled (completed/total)\n- **Progress bar 0%** - No completed issues\n- **Progress bar 100%** - All issues completed\n- **Progress bar with no issues** - Shows 0% or empty state, no division-by-zero errors\n\n#### **Tabs and Overview Tests**\n- **Header displays tabs** - Two tabs: \"Issues\" and \"Overview\", Issues active by default\n- **Clicking Overview tab** - Switches to overview content, tab becomes highlighted\n- **Overview tab renders** - Three sections: Description, Milestones, Key Metrics\n  - Description: inline editable, markdown rendering, placeholder when empty\n  - Milestones: list existing, add/edit/delete with confirmation dialog, toggle completion\n  - Key Metrics: total issues, completed, in-progress, remaining, completion percentage\n\n---\n\n### 3. Existing Test Files (35 total .spec.ts files)\n\nKey test patterns include:\n- **project-card.spec.ts** - Tests for project card display (name, status, lead, date, progress, teams)\n- **projects-create-modal.spec.ts** - Create project modal tests\n- **projects-page-filters.spec.ts** - Project filtering and sorting tests\n- Test files for: cycles, issues, team issues, sidebar, notifications, labels, etc.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Playwright Configuration\n\n**File:** `playwright.config.ts`\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Timeout: 60s per test, 10s for assertions\n- Reporter: Replay.io, JSON, HTML\n- Uses Replay Chromium device\n\n---\n\n### 5. Project Detail Components\n\n**ProjectHeader.tsx** (413 lines)\n- Inline editable project name with validation\n- Status badge dropdown (planned, in_progress, completed, cancelled)\n- Progress bar with completion percentage and text\n- Target date button (inline edit with date picker, clear button)\n- Lead selector button (searchable dropdown with members)\n- Tab buttons (Issues, Overview)\n- Data testids for all interactive elements\n\n**ProjectOverviewTab.tsx** (385 lines)\n- Description section: editable textarea, markdown rendering, placeholder\n- Milestones section:\n  - Add milestone form (name, date inputs)\n  - Milestone list with: checkbox toggle, name/date inline edit, delete button\n  - Delete confirmation dialog\n  - Empty state when no milestones\n- Key Metrics section: 5 metrics displayed (total, completed, in-progress, remaining, percentage)\n\n**ProjectDetail.tsx** (73 lines)\n- Page wrapper with header and tab content\n- Uses Redux for project state (projectDetailSlice)\n- Loading and error states\n- Switches between ProjectIssuesTab and ProjectOverviewTab based on activeTab\n\n---\n\n### 6. Seed Data (scripts/seed-db.ts)\n\nDatabase setup with sample data:\n- **Workspace:** \"Acme Corp\"\n- **Members:** Alice Johnson (alice@acme.com), Bob Smith (bob@acme.com), Carol Davis (carol@acme.com)\n- **Teams:** Engineering (ENG), Design (DES)\n- **Project:** \"V2 Launch\" (in_progress, lead: Alice, target: 2026-06-30)\n- **Issues:** 11 issues with various statuses and assignments\n- **Milestones:** 2 milestones (\"API Complete\", \"Beta Launch\")\n- **Labels:** Bug, Feature, Improvement, Documentation\n\n---\n\n### 7. Netlify Functions Related to Projects\n\n- **project-detail.ts** (209 lines) - GET project with issues, milestones, members, labels, activity\n- **update-project.ts** (194 lines) - PUT update name/status/description/targetDate/leadId with activity logging\n- **project-milestones.ts** (200 lines) - POST/PUT/DELETE milestones with activity logging\n\n---\n\n### 8. Redux State Management\n\n**projectDetailSlice.ts** (364 lines)\n\nThunks:\n- `fetchProjectDetail` - GET /api/project-detail\n- `updateProjectField` - PUT /api/update-project (name, status, description, targetDate, leadId)\n- `createMilestone` - POST /api/project-milestones\n- `updateMilestone` - PUT /api/project-milestones\n- `deleteMilestone` - DELETE /api/project-milestones\n- `updateProjectIssueStatus` - Updates progress counts automatically\n- `bulkUpdateProjectIssues` - Bulk updates with refetch\n\nState structure:\n- project (ProjectDetail)\n- issues (Issue[])\n- milestones (ProjectMilestone[])\n- members (ProjectMember[])\n- labels, activity, loading, error, selectedIssueIds\n\n---\n\n### 9. Key Data Types\n\n**ProjectDetail:**\n```typescript\nid, name, description, status, targetDate, leadId, leadName, leadEmail,\ntotalIssues, completedIssues, inProgressIssues\n```\n\n**ProjectMilestone:**\n```typescript\nid, name, targetDate, completed\n```\n\n**ProjectMember:**\n```typescript\nid, name, email\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. Test File Patterns Observed\n\nFrom `project-card.spec.ts`:\n- Helper functions: `loginViaApi`, `getProjectsData`, `createProjectViaApi`, `deleteProjectViaApi`, `createIssueViaApi`, `loginAndGoToProjects`\n- Uses data-testid attributes extensively\n- API calls for test data setup\n- localStorage session token management\n- baseURL provided by Playwright config\n- Assertions on text content, CSS classes, visibility, counts\n\n---\n\n### File Paths Summary\n\n- **Main page:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/ProjectDetail.tsx`\n- **Header component:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ProjectHeader.tsx`\n- **Overview component:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ProjectOverviewTab.tsx`\n- **Redux slice:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/projectDetailSlice.ts`\n- **API endpoints:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/project-detail.ts`, `update-project.ts`, `project-milestones.ts`\n- **Tests:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` (35 .spec.ts files)\n- **Seed data:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- **Config:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- **Documentation:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a0b70f2a50157646b (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 70011\ntool_uses: 29\nduration_ms: 64641</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"305e5aa9-79a1-4a8e-aa5e-6b1bfad647a9","uuid":"e02f002f-57c9-4ce7-a9b5-13ce1a92f1b9","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find the linear-clone app in the /repo/apps directory. I need to understand:\n1. The app directory structure (ls the top level and key subdirectories)\n2. The docs/tests.md file - read it fully, focusing on tests related to \"Project header\", \"Inline edit project name\", \"status badge\", \"target date\", \"lead\", \"Progress bar\", \"Header displays tabs\", \"Overview tab\"\n3. The existing test files (find all .spec.ts files)\n4. The playwright.config.ts\n5. The project detail page component and related components (look for project-related components)\n6. The seed data file\n7. The Netlify functions related to projects\n8. Any existing test files to understand patterns used\n\nBe thorough - read all relevant files.","agentId":"a0b70f2a50157646b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary of Linear-Clone App Exploration\n\n### 1. App Directory Structure\n\n**Top-level directories:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/` - main app directory\n- `src/` - source code\n- `tests/` - test files (.spec.ts)\n- `netlify/functions/` - backend API functions\n- `docs/` - documentation (tests.md)\n- `scripts/` - database seeding scripts\n- `public/` - static assets\n- `node_modules/` - dependencies\n- `logs/` - application logs\n\n**Key subdirectories:**\n