[2026-03-14T22:43:31.908Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VdQzRz9ZbVp5RVXS3uvWPW","type":"tool_result","content":"1829:#### Test: Project header renders all fields for an existing project\n1830-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/project/1`. Project \"Auth Rewrite\" exists with status \"In Progress\", lead \"Jane Doe\", target date 2026-04-15, and 10 issues (6 completed).\n1831-- **Expected**: The header displays the project name \"Auth Rewrite\" as an inline-editable text field. A status badge shows \"In Progress\" with appropriate styling. A progress bar shows 60% completion (6/10 issues). The target date \"Apr 15, 2026\" is displayed and inline-editable. The lead shows \"Jane Doe\" with avatar and is inline-editable.\n1832-\n1833:#### Test: Inline edit project name\n1834-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n1835-- **Action**: User clicks on the project name text, clears it, types \"Auth Rewrite v2\", and presses Enter or clicks away to confirm.\n1836-- **Expected**: The project name updates to \"Auth Rewrite v2\". The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the name change.\n1837-\n1838:#### Test: Inline edit project name — cancel edit\n1839-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n1840-- **Action**: User clicks on the project name, types \"Draft Name\", then presses Escape.\n1841-- **Expected**: The project name reverts to \"Auth Rewrite\". No change is persisted.\n1842-\n1843:#### Test: Inline edit project name — validation rejects empty name\n1844-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n1845-- **Action**: User clicks on the project name, clears the field entirely, and presses Enter.\n1846-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The project name remains \"Auth Rewrite\". No change is persisted.\n1847-\n1848:#### Test: Inline edit status badge\n1849-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project status is \"Planned\".\n1850-- **Action**: User clicks the status badge.\n1851-- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing all project statuses: \"Planned\", \"In Progress\", \"Completed\", \"Cancelled\". Each option has distinct styling/color.\n1852-\n1853:#### Test: Change project status via inline dropdown\n1854-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project status is \"Planned\". Status dropdown is open.\n1855-- **Action**: User selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown.\n1856-- **Expected**: The status badge updates to \"In Progress\" with appropriate color styling. The dropdown closes. The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the status change from \"Planned\" to \"In Progress\".\n1857-\n1858:#### Test: Change project status multiple times in sequence\n1859-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project status is \"Planned\".\n1860-- **Action**: User clicks the status badge, selects \"In Progress\". Then clicks the status badge again and selects \"Completed\".\n1861-- **Expected**: After first change, status shows \"In Progress\". After second change, status shows \"Completed\". Both changes are persisted. Two separate activity entries are created (one for each change). The progress bar and status badge update correctly each time.\n1862-\n1863:#### Test: Inline edit target date via date picker\n1864-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Target date is \"Apr 15, 2026\".\n1865-- **Action**: User clicks the target date field.\n1866-- **Expected**: A date picker opens showing the current target date pre-selected.\n1867-\n1868:#### Test: Change target date\n1869-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Target date date picker is open.\n1870-- **Action**: User selects \"May 1, 2026\" from the date picker.\n1871-- **Expected**: The target date updates to \"May 1, 2026\". The date picker closes. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created recording the target date change.\n1872-\n1873:#### Test: Clear target date\n1874-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Target date is \"Apr 15, 2026\".\n1875-- **Action**: User clicks the target date field and clicks a \"Clear\" or remove option.\n1876-- **Expected**: The target date is removed, displaying a placeholder like \"No target date\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n1877-\n1878:#### Test: Inline edit lead via searchable selector\n1879-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead is \"Jane Doe\". Workspace members include \"Jane Doe\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\".\n1880-- **Action**: User clicks on the lead field.\n1881-- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown opens listing all workspace members with avatars and names. \"Jane Doe\" is shown as currently selected.\n1882-\n1883:#### Test: Change project lead\n1884-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead selector is open.\n1885-- **Action**: User types \"Ali\" in the search field, then selects \"Alice Smith\".\n1886-- **Expected**: The lead updates to \"Alice Smith\" with her avatar. The dropdown closes. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created recording the lead change from \"Jane Doe\" to \"Alice Smith\".\n1887-\n1888:#### Test: Search lead selector filters results\n1889-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead selector is open. Members: \"Jane Doe\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\".\n1890-- **Action**: User types \"bob\" in the search field.\n1891-- **Expected**: Only \"Bob Jones\" appears in the filtered results. Other members are hidden.\n1892-\n1893:#### Test: Remove project lead\n1894-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead is \"Jane Doe\".\n1895-- **Action**: User clicks the lead field and selects a \"Remove\" or \"Unassign\" option.\n1896-- **Expected**: The lead is cleared, showing a placeholder like \"No lead\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n1897-\n1898:#### Test: Progress bar reflects issue completion accurately\n1899-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project has 10 issues total: 6 Done, 1 Cancelled, 3 In Progress.\n1900-- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 60% filled (6 completed out of 10 total). A text label or tooltip shows \"6 of 10 issues completed\" or similar.\n1901-\n1902:#### Test: Progress bar shows 0% for project with no completed issues\n1903-- **Initial state**: User is viewing a project with 5 issues, none completed.\n1904-- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 0% filled. Text indicates \"0 of 5 issues completed\" or similar.\n1905-\n1906:#### Test: Progress bar shows 100% for fully completed project\n1907-- **Initial state**: User is viewing a project with 4 issues, all with status \"Done\".\n1908-- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 100% filled with a fully colored bar.\n1909-\n1910:#### Test: Progress bar handles project with no issues\n1911-- **Initial state**: User is viewing a project with 0 issues.\n1912-- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 0% or an empty state. No division-by-zero errors occur.\n1913-\n1914:#### Test: Header displays tabs for Issues and Overview\n1915-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`.\n1916-- **Expected**: Below the header fields, two tabs are visible: \"Issues\" and \"Overview\". The \"Issues\" tab is active/selected by default.\n1917-\n1918:#### Test: Clicking Overview tab switches to overview content\n1919-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1` with the \"Issues\" tab active.\n1920-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Overview\" tab.\n1921-- **Expected**: The \"Overview\" tab becomes active/highlighted. The content area below switches to show the overview content (description, milestones, key metrics). The \"Issues\" tab is no longer highlighted.\n1922-\n1923-#### Test: Clicking Issues tab switches back to issues content\n--\n1998:- **Initial state**: User is viewi